{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You blew with Your wind.</b> From the root of נשף, for with a נשף He brought a wind that drowned them." "<b>They sank.</b> From the root of מצולות, like 'at the sound, my lips צללו' (Habakkuk 3:16)." "<b>and in mighty waters.</b> Attached to צללו, as though he said: they sank in mighty waters like lead." "<b>Like lead.</b> From the root of עפר. For the six kinds of metals, if placed under the earth, each loses a known amount over a known number of years. But lead always increases."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:41.923672944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}